aux_grating
#
# This file contains the lookup tables calibrating grating cell tilt
# angle into motor steps. A lookup table is used because the calibration
# can be non-linear and include a sinusoidal element. Cell numbers 1,2,3,4
# are the same as cells A,B,C,D. 65 degrees is the zero order reflection
# angle.
#

#
# All these lookup tables assume that the tilt vs motor steps curve for each
# cell in any position is linear with the same gradient. The gradient is
# currently chosen to be the average best fit for the B1200 and R600
# grating cells in the blaze direction +ve orientation, as measured by Chris
# Tierney and Morag Hasite at UKATC in July 2002
#
# (107.2623129 + 107.1323352) / 2.0 = 107.19732

# The curve for each position is offset by the number of motor steps
# required to bring the centre of the mask field to the centre of
# the detector field at, apparently, 65 degrees (which is the GMOS-S fold
# angle). This has been proved dependent upon both the cell and turret
# position - for this reason it should be re-calibrated whenever
# a grating cell is moved.

## Grating position B translation table
# tilt = steps /107.19732
# 65.00 required   6906   motor steps
#               Cell      Tilt      Steps
#30000020 Cell 2
2               0.0       -61.8258
2               5.0       474.1608
2               10.0      1010.1474
2               15.0      1546.1340
2               20.0      2082.1206
2               25.0      2618.1072
2               30.0      3154.0938
2               35.0      3690.0804
2               40.0      4226.0670
2               45.0      4762.0536
2               50.0      5298.0402
2               55.0      5834.0268
2               60.0      6370.0134
2               65.0      6906.0000
2               70.0      7441.9866
2               75.0      7977.9732
2               80.0      8513.9598
2               85.0      9049.9464
2               90.0      9585.9330

